    {
        "header": "3LEGO-Anything: Scene Reconstruction as Image-to-Code",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.36380/2609.36380v1/image_workflow.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Agentic scene construction, abstracted from aGPT-6-astratrajectory.Four blocks define the process: the Agent Workspace manages artifacts, the Action Space exposes agent operations, the Blender Code Structure organizes editable scene state, and the Scene Construction Workflow iterates from reference interpretation to validated final artifacts. Together, they enable executable, feedback-driven scene reconstruction.",
                "position": 527
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "header": "4LEGO-Bench: A Simulator-Grounded Benchmark for End-to-End Scene Reconstruction",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.36380/2609.36380v1/image_data_engine.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Extensible benchmark-construction pipeline.Fab assets are mined and assembled into candidate scenes; human verification triggers either remaking or annotation before acceptance. This human-in-the-loop process scales benchmark construction while retaining simulator ground truth and scene quality.",
                "position": 562
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.36380/2609.36380v1/image_data_engine.png",
